-- title:
--   Galois group of a compositum of p-extensions is a p-group
-- statement:
--   Let $E$, $F$, $L$, $N$ be number fields, with $F$, $L$, $N$ all algebras over $E$, and $N$ an algebra over both $F$ and $L$ compatibly with the $E$-structures (two scalar-tower hypotheses), and assume each of $F/E$, $L/E$, $N/E$ is Galois. Let $p$ be a prime. Suppose the automorphism group $F \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} F$ is a $p$-group and likewise $L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} L$ is a $p$-group, in the sense of `IsPGroup`: every element has order a power of $p$. Suppose further that $N$ is generated by $F$ and $L$ in the weak form that any $E$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $N$ which fixes $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,F\,N(x)$ for all $x \in F$ and $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,L\,N(y)$ for all $y \in L$ is the identity. The conclusion is that the group of $E$-algebra automorphisms of $N$ is a $p$-group, i.e. for every $\sigma \in N \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} N$ there is a natural number $n$ with $\sigma^{p^{n}} = 1$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that a compositum of two Galois $p$-extensions is again a $p$-extension, here phrased through the triviality of automorphisms fixing both subfields rather than through an explicit compositum of subfields. It is used in the Herbrand-quotient computations, where [`M4aHerbrand.finsum_div_natCard_decomp_eq_zero_of_isPGroup`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.finsum_div_natCard_decomp_eq_zero_of_isPGroup) invokes it to stay inside a $p$-group layer.
-- source:
